## Why This Is Asked

This question validates real-world CGO interop patterns, including concurrency safety, memory ownership across language boundaries, error propagation from C to Go, and data marshalling between Go slices and C arrays.

## Key Concepts

- **Memory ownership transfer** across CGO boundaries (malloc/free)
- **Thread safety** with per-call isolation for concurrent batch processing
- **Error propagation** from C to Go without memory leaks
- **Data marshalling**: converting Go []float64 to C array and JSON string back to Go

